  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Enhance the functionality for obtaining marks by modifying the get_unpacked_marks function so that it considers the method resolution order (MRO) when retrieving markers from classes. When a class inherits markers from multiple base classes (for example, classes Foo and Bar), the function should be able to merge these markers and return all of them when requested. This change addresses the issue where inheriting from multiple base classes causes one or more markers to be lost. In addition, the function should support an option to disable MRO processing so that only directly set markers are returned.",
    "hint_texts": "Update the get_unpacked_marks function in src/_pytest/mark/structures.py. Add a new keyword parameter 'consider_mro' with a default value of True. When the object is a class and consider_mro is True, iterate over the class's __mro__ to gather markers from all levels; otherwise, if consider_mro is False, only fetch markers that are directly set on the class. Make sure to normalize the marker list so that the output is consistent regardless of whether a list or a single marker is stored.",
    "entrypoint": "File: src/_pytest/mark/structures.py. Function: get_unpacked_marks. Modify the function signature (around the original implementation starting at line 355) and update the body to handle the consider_mro parameter appropriately for classes and non-class objects.",
