  "feature2": {
    "prompt": "Update the behavior for storing marks by modifying the store_mark function so that it only considers directly assigned markers when adding a new mark. This means that store_mark should invoke the marker retrieval function with MRO processing disabled. By doing so, the function will avoid merging inherited markers when storing a new one, thereby preserving the intended behavior for marker assignment on classes. This change ensures that new markers are added without inadvertently including markers from superclasses.",
    "hint_texts": "In the file src/_pytest/mark/structures.py, locate the store_mark function and update its call to get_unpacked_marks by passing the parameter consider_mro set to False. This small but critical change will limit the marker retrieval to markers that are directly on the object, and not those inherited through the MRO. Ensure that the final pytestmark attribute reflects only the directly applied markers along with the newly stored mark.",
    "entrypoint": "File: src/_pytest/mark/structures.py. Function: store_mark. Modify the existing code (around line 388 as indicated in the diff) so that the call to get_unpacked_marks includes the argument consider_mro=False.",
